# Migrations are hashed by the runner. Git's autocrlf would rewrite them on a
# Windows clone and change the checksum, so they are pinned to LF everywhere:
# the server is Linux, and a database created on either platform must start on
# both. The checksum also normalises line endings as a second guard.
*.sql text eol=lf

# Anything that is compared byte for byte, or executed on the server.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
